"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nThis is a reality show where Park Bo-gum holds a barber's license and opens a hair salon in a rural village.  \nSince he is with his close friends Lee Sang-yi and Kwak Dong-yeon, their chemistry is natural and not forced.  \nListening to the stories of the elderly while trimming their hair is all there is to this program.  \n\nThe review that it gives harmless fun without sensational editing or forced high-tension was absolutely spot on.  \nIt's just a hair salon newly opened in the countryside, but watching it makes one's heart soften.  \n\nIt was heartwarming to see them trimming hair and even serving a warm meal.  \nThe rustic dialect and laughter felt as if they were being transmitted right out of the screen.  \n\nI've always liked this kind of healing content.  \nWatching reality shows that flow calmly without any major incidents makes me feel like the fatigue of the day is melting away.  \n\nBogum Magical was a program that filled exactly that kind of healing.  \nIt was heartwarming all the way through, and it made my heart feel warm.  \n\nSince Season 2 is coming in the second half of the year, I'm already looking forward to it."